cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this atlas and the relevant task entry. Record the atlas commit, entry date,
  archive revision and model identifier used; this citation does not identify every network snapshot.
  Code has a separate MIT licence; the dataset licence below covers original atlas material.
type: dataset
title: "Mechanistic Interpretability Circuit Atlas"
abstract: >-
  A living collection of small-network circuit studies for algorithmic tasks, with hand-built references, partly trained and
  from-scratch transformers, and external recurrent-model zoo snapshots. Entries report task performance separately from
  substitution and complement-resampling evidence, retaining failures, limited coverage and unresolved mechanisms.
authors:
  - alias: jc1122
repository-code: "https://github.com/jc1122/mechanistic-interpretability-circuit-atlas"
url: "https://github.com/jc1122/mechanistic-interpretability-circuit-atlas"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/jc1122/circuit-atlas-nets"
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-11-08"
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - transformer circuits
  - algorithmic tasks
  - hand-built transformers
  - grokking
  - recurrent neural networks
  - reproducibility
